===Etymology===
From {{inh|ang|gmw-pro|*fregnan}}, {{inh|ang|gem-pro|*frehnaną}}.

{{rel-top|Cognates:}}
Cognate with {{cog|osx|fregnan}}, {{cog|non|fregna}}, {{cog|got|𐍆𐍂𐌰𐌹𐌷𐌽𐌰𐌽}}, and related to {{cog|goh|frāga}} ({{cog|de|Frage}}). The Indo-European root also gave {{cog|peo|𐎠𐎱𐎼𐎿𐎶||ts=aparsam|I asked}}, {{cog|sga|arcaid}}, {{cog|wlm|archaf}}, {{cog|xcl|հարց}}, {{cog|xto|prak-}}, {{cog|txb|prek-}}. {{rel-bottom}}

